{"reference": "E", "saved_D_answer": "A", "saved_D_rationale": "Answer: A\nReason: The chest X-ray shows complete opacification (white-out) of the left hemithorax with a significant mediastinal shift to the right, which is characteristic of a massive pleural effusion pushing structures away from the affected side. In contrast, atelectasis would cause a shift toward the opacity, and pneumonia typically does not cause such a dramatic contralateral shift without associated volume loss or effusion."}
